{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they said to him, Where.</b> The Sages, blessed be their memory: a point is placed on the aleph to teach you that they asked even of Sarah, on behalf of Abraham, 'where is he'; and it would have been fitting to point the lamed and to interpret the written form, which is the principal thing, except that there is a small zakef on the letter lamed and it would have become intermingled with the point, and therefore they pointed the aleph and not the letter lamed." "<b>And it appears</b> to me further regarding this, that besides this word being given for midrashic interpretation, there is yet an inner meaning in it that is necessary and compelling. For these angels hinted to Abraham the matter of the influx that flows down from above to the attributes (middot), and from the attributes to the separate intellects, and from the separate intellects to the lower world. For after Abraham was sanctified and sealed with the sign of the holy covenant, the angels wished to tell him wondrous secrets of wisdom concerning the influx. For they — like all the rest of the separate beings — all draw power from the tenth, and the tenth by way of the line, and the line from the aleph. And therefore a point was placed on the aleph to hint that they transmitted to him knowledge concerning the influx: how it flows down from the aleph to the yod by way of the line, and from the yod to the intellects, and from the intellects to the prophet, to make known the future — what El has wrought in the lower world. And therefore they make the matter known and announce it to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:14.363152090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}